    {
      "type": "text", "id": "failure_body", "x": 50, "y": 845, "width": 690, "height": 220,
      "text": "❌ BAD (without outbox):  await SaveChangesAsync(); await bus.PublishAsync(...);  ← two ops, can fail independently.\n\nFailures the outbox makes impossible:\n\n  ●  Bus publish fails mid-handler\n      → tx hasn't committed yet → ROLLBACK on exception → neither row persists → handler errors out, client retries cleanly.\n\n  ●  Process crashes between SaveChanges and bus.PublishAsync\n      → impossible: there IS no separate publish step. Wolverine staged the envelope inside the same tx. Both rows are there OR neither is.\n\n  ●  Bus publish succeeds, save commit fails\n      → impossible: there's only one commit. If it fails, no envelope exists. If it succeeds, both rows are durable.\n\n  ●  Bus is down when dispatcher tries to flush\n      → envelope stays in wolverine.outgoing_envelopes. Dispatcher retries with backoff. As soon as bus is back, drains.\n\n  ●  Dispatcher process crashes after sending but before deleting envelope\n      → at-least-once: a duplicate delivery. Consumer must be idempotent (status guard pattern). See OrderService.Application/EventHandlers/.",
      "originalText": "❌ BAD (without outbox):  await SaveChangesAsync(); await bus.PublishAsync(...);  ← two ops, can fail independently.\n\nFailures the outbox makes impossible:\n\n  ●  Bus publish fails mid-handler\n      → tx hasn't committed yet → ROLLBACK on exception → neither row persists → handler errors out, client retries cleanly.\n\n  ●  Process crashes between SaveChanges and bus.PublishAsync\n      → impossible: there IS no separate publish step. Wolverine staged the envelope inside the same tx. Both rows are there OR neither is.\n\n  ●  Bus publish succeeds, save commit fails\n      → impossible: there's only one commit. If it fails, no envelope exists. If it succeeds, both rows are durable.\n\n  ●  Bus is down when dispatcher tries to flush\n      → envelope stays in wolverine.outgoing_envelopes. Dispatcher retries with backoff. As soon as bus is back, drains.\n\n  ●  Dispatcher process crashes after sending but before deleting envelope\n      → at-least-once: a duplicate delivery. Consumer must be idempotent (status guard pattern). See OrderService.Application/EventHandlers/.",
      "fontSize": 11, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#374151", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0,
      "seed": 500005, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 500006,
      "isDeleted": false, "groupIds": [], "boundElements": null, "link": null, "locked": false, "containerId": null, "lineHeight": 1.3
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle", "id": "config_panel", "x": 30, "y": 1110, "width": 1140, "height": 130,
      "strokeColor": "#1e293b", "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0,
      "seed": 600001, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 600002,
      "isDeleted": false, "groupIds": [], "boundElements": [{"id":"config_t","type":"text"}], "link": null, "locked": false, "roundness": {"type": 3}
    },
    {
      "type": "text", "id": "config_t", "x": 45, "y": 1125, "width": 1110, "height": 110,
      "text": "// each service's Api/Program.cs — the configuration that makes it work\nbuilder.Host.UseWolverine(opts => {\n    opts.PersistMessagesWithSqlServer(connStr, \"wolverine\");      // or .PersistMessagesWithPostgresql for Shipping\n    opts.UseEntityFrameworkCoreTransactions();                    // bridge to EF's tx\n    opts.Policies.AutoApplyTransactions();                        // wrap handlers in EF tx\n    opts.Policies.UseDurableOutboxOnAllSendingEndpoints();        // stage outgoing into wolverine.outgoing_envelopes\n});\nbuilder.Services.AddResourceSetupOnStartup();                     // auto-create wolverine schema + tables on app boot",
      "originalText": "// each service's Api/Program.cs — the configuration that makes it work\nbuilder.Host.UseWolverine(opts => {\n    opts.PersistMessagesWithSqlServer(connStr, \"wolverine\");      // or .PersistMessagesWithPostgresql for Shipping\n    opts.UseEntityFrameworkCoreTransactions();                    // bridge to EF's tx\n    opts.Policies.AutoApplyTransactions();                        // wrap handlers in EF tx\n    opts.Policies.UseDurableOutboxOnAllSendingEndpoints();        // stage outgoing into wolverine.outgoing_envelopes\n});\nbuilder.Services.AddResourceSetupOnStartup();                     // auto-create wolverine schema + tables on app boot",
      "fontSize": 11, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#22c55e", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0,
      "seed": 600003, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 600004,
      "isDeleted": false, "groupIds": [], "boundElements": null, "link": null, "locked": false, "containerId": null, "lineHeight": 1.3
